        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "54ca4741-1c34-5b43-9498-0641277c3fb7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Desaga, Robert Wilhelm Bunsen, Michael Faraday, Georg Lunge, Ferdinand Cohn\n- Organizations: University of Heidelberg, University of Breslau\n- Products: Bunsen burner, laboratory burner\n- Topics: electromagnetism, electrochemistry\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Faraday was an English scientist born on 22 September 1791 and died on 25 August 1867.\n- Michael Faraday contributed to the study of electromagnetism and electrochemistry.\n- In 1855, Peter Desaga perfected an earlier laboratory burner design by Michael Faraday into the Bunsen burner.\n- Peter Desaga was a German instrument maker at the University of Heidelberg who worked with Robert Wilhelm Bunsen.\n- Robert Wilhelm Bunsen and his laboratory assistant Peter Desaga developed the Bunsen burner as an improvement on laboratory burners then in use.\n- In 1859, Georg Lunge graduated from the University of Breslau for work with Ferdinand Cohn after studying at Heidelberg under Robert Bunsen and at Breslau.",
